# Suppressions are the exception, not the habit. Each entry states why the code
# path is unreachable here and what has to happen before the line can be deleted.

# deepmerge-ts 7.1.5 — stack exhaustion on recursive object graphs.
#
# Reached only as @prisma/client -> prisma -> @prisma/config -> deepmerge-ts,
# where it merges Prisma's own config files at CLI start-up. No request data
# reaches that merge, and the service never calls it at runtime.
#
# It cannot be selected away safely. `prisma` is an *optional peer* of
# @prisma/client, so npm installs the CLI into the production image and
# `--omit=dev` cannot exclude it. Prisma 7.8.0 pins deepmerge-ts to an exact
# 7.1.5; forcing the major-version 8 package would be an unverified Prisma CLI
# change.
#
# Remove when a Prisma release bumps @prisma/config onto deepmerge-ts 8.
CVE-2026-40345
